Q: Convert a $lookup stage from localField-foreignField to let-pipeline A: <p>From <a href="https://mongodocs.github.io/reference/operator/aggregation/lookup.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com#use-lookup-with-an-array" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Use $lookup with an Array</a>,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If the <code>localField</code> is an array, you can match the array elements against a scalar <code>foreignField</code> without an <code>$unwind</code> stage.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Although the documentation mentioned on <code>localField</code>, but this seems <code>foreignField</code> has the same functionality that MongoDB will flatten and traverse the element to do the equality match.</p>
<hr />
<p>If you keen on <code>pipeline</code>, you should flatten the <code>forms.version.formId</code> array via <code>$reduce</code> operator. After flatten the array, use <code>$in</code> operator to filter the document that the <code>frmFormId</code> value is within the array.</p>
<pre><code>db.results.aggregate([
  {
    &quot;$match&quot;: {
      &quot;_id&quot;: 2025082800100
    }
  },
  {
    $lookup: {
      from: &quot;flows&quot;,
      let: {
        frmFormId: &quot;$orginalFormId&quot;
      },
      pipeline: [
        {
          $match: {
            $expr: {
              $in: [
                &quot;$$frmFormId&quot;,
                {
                  $reduce: {
                    input: &quot;$forms.version.formId&quot;,
                    initialValue: [],
                    in: {
                      $concatArrays: [
                        &quot;$$value&quot;,
                        &quot;$$this&quot;
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      as: &quot;flowId&quot;
    }
  }
])
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://mongoplayground.net/p/ebpZ3NgHuOB" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo @ Mongo Playground</a></p>
<hr />
<p>And of course you can work the <code>$lookup</code> stage with both <code>localField</code>-<code>foreignField</code> and <code>let</code>-<code>pipeline</code> together.</p>
<pre><code>db.results.aggregate([
  {
    &quot;$match&quot;: {
      &quot;_id&quot;: 2025082800100
    }
  },
  {
    $lookup: {
      from: &quot;flows&quot;,
      let: {
        // Declare variable and store field value from collection
      },
      localField: &quot;orginalFormId&quot;, 
      foreignField: &quot;forms.version.formId&quot;,
      pipeline: [
        // $match stage for additional filter criteria
      ],
      as: &quot;flowId&quot;
    }
  }
])
</code></pre>
